$\n\n$x^{13} = x \\cdot x^{12} = x(4x+2) = 4x^2+2x = (4,2,0)$\n\n$x^{14} = x \\cdot x^{13} = x(4x^2+2x) = 4x^3+2x^2 = 4(4x+4)+2x^2 = 16x+16+2x^2 = x+1+2x^2 = 2x^2+x+1 = (2,1,1)$\n\n$x^{15} = x \\cdot x^{14} = x(2x^2+x+1) = 2x^3+x^2+x = 2(4x+4)+x^2+x = 8x+8+x^2+x = 3x+3+x^2+x = x^2+4x+3 = (1,4,3)$\n\n$x^{16} = x \\cdot x^{15} = x(x^2+4x+3) = x^3+4x^2+3x = (4x+4)+4x^2+3x = 4x^2+7x+4 = 4x^2+2x+4 = (4,2,4)$\n\n$x^{17} = x \\cdot x^{16} = x(4x^2+2x+4) = 4x^3+2x^2+4x = 4(4x+4)+2x^2+4x = 16x+16+2x^2+4x = x+1+2x^2+4x = 2x^2+5x+1 = 2x^2+1 = (2,0,1)$\n\nHmm, I need $x^2+1 = (1,0,1)$. Let me keep going but this is tedious. Let me think about whether there's a smarter approach.\n\nActually, let me just continue the computation carefully. I need $(1,0,1)$.\n\n$x^{18} = x \\cdot x^{17} = x(2x^2+1) = 2x^3+x = 2(4x+4)+x = 8x+8+x = 3x+3+x = 4x+3 = (0,4,3)$\n\n$x^{19} = x \\cdot x^{18} = x(4x+3) = 4x^2+3x = (4,3,0)$\n\n$x^{20} = x \\cdot x^{19} = x(4x^2+3x) = 4x^3+3x^2 = 4(4x+4)+3x^2 = 16x+16+3x^2 = x+1+3x^2 = 3x^2+x+1 = (3,1,1)$\n\n$x^{21} = x \\cdot x^{20} = x(3x^2+x+1) = 3x^3+x^2+x = 3(4x+4)+x^2+x = 12x+12+x^2+x = 2x+2+x^2+x = x^2+3x+2 = (1,3,2)$\n\n$x^{22} = x \\cdot x^{21} = x(x^2+3x+2) = x^3+3x^2+2x = (4x+4)+3x^2+2x = 3x^2+6x+4 = 3x^2+x+4 = (3,1,4)$\n\n$x^{23} = x \\cdot x^{22} = x(3x^2+x+4) = 3x^3+x^2+4x = 3(4x+4)+x^2+4x = 12x+12+x^2+4x = 2x+2+x^2+4x = x^2+6x+2 = x^2+x+2 = (1,1,2)$\n\n$x^{24} = x \\cdot x^{23} = x(x^2+x+2) = x^3+x^2+2x = (4x+4)+x^2+2x = x^2+6x+4 = x^2+x+4 = (1,1,4)$\n\n$x^{25} = x \\cdot x^{24} = x(x^2+x+4) = x^3+x^2+4x = (4x+4)+x^2+4x = x^2+8x+4 = x^2+3x+4 = (1,3,4)$\n\n$x^{26} = x \\cdot x^{25} = x(x^2+3x+4) = x^3+3x^2+4x = (4x+4)+3x^2+4x = 3x^2+8x+4 = 3x^2+3x+4 = (3,3,4)$\n\n$x^{27} = x \\cdot x^{26} = x(3x^2+3x+4) = 3x^3+3x^2+4x = 3(4x+4)+3x^2+4x = 12x+12+3x^2+4x = 2x+2+3x^2+4x = 3x^2+6x+2 = 3x^2+x+2 = (3,1,2)$\n\n$x^{28} = x \\cdot x^{27} = x(3x^2+x+2) = 3x^3+x^2+2x = 3(4x+4)+x^2+2x = 12x+12+x^2+2x = 2x+2+x^2+2x = x^2+4x+2 = (1,4,2)$\n\n$x^{29} = x \\cdot x^{28} = x(x^2+4x+2) = x^3+4x^2+2x = (4x+4)+4x^2+2x = 4x^2+6x+4 = 4x^2+x+4 = (4,1,4)$\n\n$x^{30} = x \\cdot x^{29} = x(4x^2+x+4) = 4x^3+x^2+4x = 4(4x+4)+x^2+4x = 16x+16+x^2+4x = x+1+x^2+4x = x^2+5x+1 = x^2+1 = (1,0,1)$\n\nSo $x^{30} = x^2 + 1$.\n\nTherefore $\\operatorname{dlog}_x(x^2+1) = 30$.\n\nLet me verify this is consistent. The multiplicative group has order 124. 30 < 124, good. Let me double-check the computation of $x^{30}$.\n\nLet me re-verify a few key steps to make sure I didn't make an arithmetic error.\n\n$x^3 = 4x+4$. ✓ (since $x^3 + x + 1 = 0$ means $x^3 = -x-1 = 4x+4$)\n\n$x^{29} = (4,1,4) = 4x^2+x+4$.\n$x^{30} = x \\cdot (4x^2+x+4) = 4x^3 + x^2 + 4x$.\n$4x^3 = 4(4x+4) = 16x+16 = x+1$ (mod 5).\nSo $x^{30} = (x+1) + x^2 + 4x = x^2 + 5x + 1 = x^2 + 1$. ✓\n\nLet me also verify $x^{29}$ by checking $x^{28}$.\n\n$x^{27} = (3,1,2) = 3x^2+x+2$.\n$x^{28} = x(3x^2+x+2) = 3x^3+x^2+2x = 3(4x+4)+x^2+2x = (12x+12)+x^2+2x = (2x+2)+x^2+2x = x^2+4x+2 = (1,4,2)$. ✓\n\n$x^{29} = x(x^2+4x+2) = x^3+4x^2+2x = (4x+4)+4x^2+2x = 4x^2+6x+4 = 4x^2+x+4 = (4,1,4)$. ✓\n\nGreat, so the answer is 30.\n\nActually, let me verify a few more intermediate steps to be safe, since one error propagates.\n\n$x^4 = x \\cdot x^3 = x(4x+4) = 4x^2+4x = (4,4,0)$. ✓\n\n$x^5 = x(4x^2+4x) = 4x^3+4x^2 = 4(4x+4)+4x^2 = (16x+16)+4x^2 = (x+1)+4x^2 = 4x^2+x+1 = (4,1,1)$. ✓\n\nLet me verify by a different route. Let me check $x^{10}$ and $x^{20}$ and $x^{30}$ using $x^{30} = x^{20} \\cdot x^{10}$.\n\n$x^{10} = (3,3,3) = 3x^2+3x+3$.\n$x^{20} = (3,1,1) = 3x^2+x+1$.\n\n$x^{30}$ should equal $x^{20} \\cdot x^{10} = (3x^2+x+1)(3x^2+3x+3)$.\n\nLet me compute this product:\n$(3x^2+x+1)(3x^2+3x+3)$\n$= 9x^4 + 9x^3 + 9x^2 + 3x^3 + 3x^2 + 3x + 3x^2 + 3x + 3$\n$= 9x^4 + (9+3)x^3 + (9+3+3)x^2 + (3+3)x + 3$\n$= 9x^4 + 12x^3 + 15x^2 + 6x + 3$\n$= 4x^4 + 2x^3 + 0x^2 + x + 3$ (mod 5)\n\nNow reduce: $x^3 = 4x+4$, $x^4 = x \\cdot x^3 = x(4x+4) = 4x^2+4x$.\n$4x^4 = 4(4x^2+4x) = 16x^2+16x = x^2+x$.\n$2x^3 = 2(4x+4) = 8x+8 = 3x+3$.\n\nSo $4x^4 + 2x^3 + x + 3 = (x^2+x) + (3x+3) + x + 3 = x^2 + (1+3+1)x + (3+3) = x^2 + 5x + 6 = x^2 + 0x + 1 = x^2+1$. ✓\n\nSo $x^{30} = x^2+1$ is confirmed by two independent computations.\n\nThe answer is $\\operatorname{dlog}_x(x^2+1) = 30$.", "tool_calls": [], "created_at": 1787230785}
